    "turn_text": "at that time is when Obama was in office. And so I would have a lot of people come up to me adults be like, you can be president one day. And I think they were just saying that because they saw me do a speech and Obama and black and I used to have a bus cut and all this stuff, you know? So, like, people have been telling me to run for office kind of a lot of my life, but I never really wanted to do it. I guess I thought maybe in the future, but I just, you know, had other things I wanted to do. I actually wanted to work in music mainly, and I did. I worked on music and politics kind of at the same time. But that's what I saw myself doing. You know, I went to an art school for a middle school and high school. It was a public arts magnet school. And so I was a jazz drummer there. And then I also helped plan a lot of concerts as part of the reason I went on to go work on music festivals. And so that was kind of my trajectory. That's what I was focused on. And I worked the campaign at Fresh 18 for Hillary and Florida. And at the end of that campaign, I was like, all right, we're going to win this. I'm going to go back to college, and then I'm going to do some music stuff. Well, we did it win that. A plot",
