    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95659.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 142,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Well, people are very demoralized in our state right now. We are being governed by a very far right wing movement that the book stops with the census in our state. But it really is a movement across the state of local elected state representatives and all these people who want to consolidate power for one person. And that person's using that power to kind of a press certain groups of people. And so that's kind of what's going on right now. We see with the don't say gay law, right? We see it with a book banning in our state, the role black of gun laws in our state, the attacks on unions in our state, the attacks on the ability for localities to do anything about housing in our state. Like there's so much going on right now that really has this authoritarian bend. And we've done a lot to try to prevent it. And we've been successful in some part, so we haven't been successful in a lot of them. And so that leads people to kind of take a step back and say like, what the hell is going on? And you've seen this like exodus of immigrants and queer people from the state of Florida, other states, because they're scared for their lives. And I always like to tell people like we hear people talk about Florida, they talk about culture wars, which yes, that's a big part of it. But it's not just a culture words that there's like real violence going on in our state right now that is encouraged and supported by people like Ron and Santa. So that's like the context.",
