    "turn_idx": 144,
    "turn_text": "Despite all of that, there's still And we're still a state of millions and millions of like poor and working class people who are just like want to live, and we love our state. You know, I love the state of Florida, it's my home. Like I love Orlando, it's my home. So a lot of young people aren't to moralize with the state of Florida, but they're fighting back. And we see it in movements across the entire state. We see it in young people running for office. We see a lot of mutual aid going on, direct action, protests, et cetera, because everyone has a different way of being involved in this. thing that we're doing. And that gives me a lot of hope. We have a, you know, look at the last two special elections in Florida, Democrats who flipped red seats, the blue seats, the biggest city in Florida, Jacksonville, flipped from a red mayor to a blue one, Donna Degan, in Orlando, Florida. We had a special election just a few months ago. We elected Tom Keene, the Santa's won that seat by like, over 12 points just like last year. And this year, Tom Keene won by I think like four or five. So it just shows that like we're going in the right direction. The cards are stacked up against us. It's hard as hell, not",
