    "turn_text": "So essentially, you have a party that's in the majority and that's in the minority. So the majority would be like, if you have one more person in the House of Representatives, you being a majority right now, and the US Congress Republicans have a majority, very slim one, very slim, which means there's not a lot of room for error. If there's a few Republicans, I think right now it's like, two or three. If two or three Republicans joined Democrats on a bill, we could pass the bill. And that's not a place that you want to be if you're in the majority because it means that you really have to have everybody in line. And that can be hard, especially these days. So if you have a super majority, That means you have so many more people than the minority party that has in that body that you can steamroll anything you want without even talking with the Democrats, without even talking with the party that's in the minority. You don't even need to care about what they say, what they do, they can blab all they want, but you have so many more people than they do that you could lose a few. And it doesn't matter. You're getting what you want past. So that's why it's so important is it gives us more of a voice because the more that that majority is slim, the more that our voices are respected and heard and included in the legislative process. But right now in Tallahassee in Florida, the Republicans, Democrats don't have enough of a voice to change the damn temperature of the building, like legislation. And the reason why is because they outnumber us by so much, they don't even need to listen to us. They don't even need to engage with us. And I'm not saying they don't at all. Sometimes they do. But when you break them, the super majority gives you the ability to do even more. And in our state right now, we need to read, damn,",
