    "turn_idx": 181,
    "turn_text": "I think it's a pro. And we're just bad ass. But it makes it difficult to swallow this pill, which is our system. is set in a way where we are given very binary choices, especially at the presidential level. We can complain about it. I've done a lot of traveling last year to countries where there's multiple parties and you see a lot of, I don't know, it feels like a lot of their systems work in a better way than ours do, even though there's multiple parties and it gives people the opportunity for collaboration without feeling guilty with working with other people. You actually see more bipartisanship. We're not going to have like a multi-party system tomorrow, this year, next year, or in a few years. If there's something you want to work towards, you have to build political power and political will to make that happen. If you step away, it'll never happen. Okay. But right now, it's super binary. And I get, I think a lot of frustration we're seeing around voting for the president in this election is I think a lot of people are just frustrated with the fact that you get like two choices and that's it. And I get that. But it also is the situation as it is. I believe, from my vantage point, the things I've seen that President Biden is eons better than President Trump on every issue I care about. And for me, it's not too much of a lesser of two evils kind of thing because I've seen like the work save lives in my community. And",
