    "turn_text": "And what I'll say is this, the foundation of it, at least I don't want to say for everybody, but for a lot of people comes from a really good place that I agree with actually. And so the concern is, TikTok gathers a lot of our data and the parent company is pretty much falls under the rules and laws of the Chinese Communist Party in Beijing because it is a Chinese-owned company. And I think the concern is, you know, the laws in China with this government, with this government say like if they want data on any American, they can direct a company to give it to them and they have to because they fall under the laws of the CCP. And that is concerning, like 100%. That's very concerning. But we have no evidence that that's happened thus far. but it could happen. So I think that's like the first thing is like it could happen. Hey, that's concerning to me. However, I'm also on the same token. I'm also concerned about domestic companies and",
